meta {
  name: Sync news feed blogposts
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/news-feed/blogposts
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  x-xtm-hub-token: {{xtm-hub-token}}
}

docs {
  Webhook called by n8n each time a blog post is published, edited or unpublished. It is only a trigger: the request
  body is ignored, the Hub fetches the latest blog posts of each product (OpenCTI and OpenAEV) itself and reconciles
  the news feed. A post tagged for both products gives two items, and every product is synchronized on its own: its
  own blog API call, safeguard and transaction.

  Ensure xtm-hub-token is defined in environment. It is the system token: the sync runs as the system user.

  Answers:
  - 200 once every product is committed, with the totals and the same counts for each product:
    {
      "created": 2, "updated": 0, "dropped": 1, "provisionedPlatforms": 12,
      "products": {
        "opencti": { "created": 1, "updated": 0, "dropped": 1, "provisionedPlatforms": 12 },
        "openaev": { "created": 1, "updated": 0, "dropped": 0, "provisionedPlatforms": 0 }
      }
    }
    provisionedPlatforms is 0 for a product whose platforms do not support blog posts yet (OpenAEV is still disabled).
  - 401, with no body, when the token is missing or wrong (identical in both cases)
  - 429 when the rate limit is exceeded (30 requests per minute per IP)
  - 500 with { "message": "Unable to synchronize blog posts" } when at least one product fails. Nothing of the failing
    product is applied, but the other products are: calling the endpoint again fixes the failed one. The details
    (product, post id) are in the Hub logs.
}
